AMX XSAVE state: fix the TILECFG image layout, the TILEDATA row count and the TILEDATA XINUSE test

Three defects in cpu/xsave.cc's AMX component handlers, all visible through
STTILECFG (which is xsave_tilecfg_state) and XSAVE/XRSTOR with RFBM bits 17/18:

1. xsave_tilecfg_state wrote tilecfg[n].rows into the 16-bit colsb slots
   (bytes 16..31) and tilecfg[n].bytes_per_row into the row bytes (48..55) —
   the reverse of the architectural image and of configure_tiles' own read
   side (vmm16u(8+n) = bytes_per_row, vmmubyte(48+n) = rows). A saved image
   therefore did not round-trip through LDTILECFG, and STTILECFG after
   LDTILECFG returned a different image from the one loaded.

2. xsave_tiledata_state / xrstor_tiledata_state iterated
   row < BX_TILE_REGISTERS (8) instead of BX_TILE_MAX_ROWS (16), so only the
   first 4 KiB of the 8 KiB TILEDATA component was saved or restored; rows
   8..15 of every tile stayed stale in the save area / the registers.

3. xsave_tiledata_state_xinuse returned tile_use_tracker == 0, i.e. reported
   the component IN USE exactly when no tile had been touched, which inverts
   XSTATE_BV[18] in every XSAVE and makes XSAVEOPT/XSAVEC skip live tile data.

Found by this crate's differential suite the day AMX was first compiled into
the vendored core; see docs/backend-differences.md §4l/§4m/§4o. Still present
on upstream master as of 2026-09-12.

The hunks below are deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

--- a/cpu/xsave.cc
+++ b/cpu/xsave.cc
@@ -1152,8 +1152,8 @@ void BX_CPU_C::xsave_tilecfg_state(bxInstruction_c *i, bx_address offset)
     tilecfg.vmmubyte(1) = BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->start_row;

     for (unsigned n=0; n < 8; n++) {
-      tilecfg.vmm16u(8+n)    = BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tilecfg[n].rows;
-      tilecfg.vmmubyte(48+n) = BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tilecfg[n].bytes_per_row;
+      tilecfg.vmm16u(8+n)    = BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tilecfg[n].bytes_per_row;
+      tilecfg.vmmubyte(48+n) = BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tilecfg[n].rows;
     }
   }

@@ -1185,7 +1185,7 @@ void BX_CPU_C::xsave_tiledata_state(bxInstruction_c *i, bx_address offset)
   bx_address asize_mask = i->asize_mask();

   for (unsigned tile=0; tile < BX_TILE_REGISTERS; tile++) {
-    for (unsigned row=0; row < BX_TILE_REGISTERS; row++) {
+    for (unsigned row=0; row < BX_TILE_MAX_ROWS; row++) {
       write_virtual_zmmword(i->seg(), (offset+(tile*BX_TILE_MAX_ROWS+row)*64) & asize_mask, &(BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tile[tile].row[row]));
     }
   }
@@ -1196,7 +1196,7 @@ void BX_CPU_C::xrstor_tiledata_state(bxInstruction_c *i, bx_address offset)
   bx_address asize_mask = i->asize_mask();

   for (unsigned tile=0; tile < BX_TILE_REGISTERS; tile++) {
-    for (unsigned row=0; row < BX_TILE_REGISTERS; row++) {
+    for (unsigned row=0; row < BX_TILE_MAX_ROWS; row++) {
       read_virtual_zmmword(i->seg(), (offset+(tile*BX_TILE_MAX_ROWS+row)*64) & asize_mask, &(BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tile[tile].row[row]));
     }
     BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->set_tile_used(tile);
@@ -1213,7 +1213,7 @@ void BX_CPU_C::xrstor_init_tiledata_state(void)

 bool BX_CPU_C::xsave_tiledata_state_xinuse(void)
 {
-  return (BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tile_use_tracker == 0);  // all tiles are zero
+  return (BX_CPU_THIS_PTR amx->tile_use_tracker != 0);
 }

 #endif
